1482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (A practical application of this autonomy is evident in predictive maintenance systems. Agentic AI agents continuously monitor industrial equipment via IoT sensors, ingesting multivariate time-series data. The agent autonomously identifies precursor signatures of potential equipment failure by employing advanced time-series forecasting and anomaly detection algorithms \(e.g., LSTMs, Isolation Forests\). Its decision engine, often a reinforcement learning \(RL\) policy network, then autonomously schedules maintenance actions \(e.g., initiating a work order via an API, dispatching a technician through a logistics system\). This eliminates the latency of human analysis, significantly reduces Mean Time To Repair \(MTTR\), and minimizes unscheduled downtime. Through iterative refinement of their RL policy based on actual maintenance outcomes and equipment lifespan, these agents continuously improve their predictive accuracy and operational efficiency.)
/E (A practical application of this autonomy is evident in predictive maintenance systems. Agentic AI agents continuously monitor industrial equipment via IoT sensors, ingesting multivariate time-series data. The agent autonomously identifies precursor signatures of potential equipment failure by employing advanced time-series forecasting and anomaly detection algorithms \(e.g., LSTMs, Isolation Forests\). Its decision engine, often a reinforcement learning \(RL\) policy network, then autonomously schedules maintenance actions \(e.g., initiating a work order via an API, dispatching a technician through a logistics system\). This eliminates the latency of human analysis, significantly reduces Mean Time To Repair \(MTTR\), and minimizes unscheduled downtime. Through iterative refinement of their RL policy based on actual maintenance outcomes and equipment lifespan, these agents continuously improve their predictive accuracy and operational efficiency.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
