/K [3]
>>
endobj
1651 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The system initiates its cycle by meticulously acquiring data from disparate, multi-modal sources. This encompasses high-velocity, real-time streams \(e.g., IoT telemetry, financial market feeds, API responses\) alongside vast historical archives \(e.g., enterprise data lakes, archival databases, web logs\). The ingested data modalities are diverse, ranging from highly structured relational schemas to semi-structured JSON/XML, and crucially, unstructured formats such as natural language text, image sequences, and audio streams.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1652 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A critical initial phase involves a robust data pipeline for cleansing, pre-processing, and normalization. This entails rigorous outlier detection, imputation strategies for missing values, noise reduction via filtering algorithms, and feature scaling \(e.g., Z-score normalization\) to ensure data homogeneity and prevent gradient explosion in deep learning models. Specialized pre-processing units are paramount for unstructured data: LLMs transform textual data into high-dimensional embedding vectors for semantic understanding, while convolutional neural networks \(CNNs\) process image data into feature representations. This foundational step ensures data fidelity and suitability for subsequent analytical stages.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
