1669 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This phase constitutes the core of the agent's autonomy. Based on the insights and predictions derived from pattern recognition, the decision-making engine \(often powered by a learned policy from Reinforcement Learning, a sophisticated planning algorithm, or an expert system with dynamically updated rules\) computes the optimal course of action. This involves evaluating potential outcomes, considering predefined utility functions \(e.g., cost minimization, performance maximization\), and selecting the action that best aligns with the agent's objectives.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1670 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The chosen action is then instantiated via effector modules that interface directly with the operational environment. These effectors can trigger diverse actions: executing API calls to external systems \(e.g., initiating a financial transaction, adjusting cloud resource allocation\), dispatching commands to physical robotic systems, or orchestrating Robotic Process Automation \(RPA\) bots to perform tasks within legacy applications \(e.g., automating data entry, generating reports\). The actions are not mere outputs; they are interventions designed to directly influence the system's state and achieve the agent's goals without necessitating human confirmation for every step.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
